m have  a prominent speaking gig even if they  try to shut the door in his face just  like they did in 2008 which led Ron Paul  to run his own counter convention which  drew 13,000 people across town in  Minneapolis even if they do this the the  injection of Ron Paul ISM in the  Republican Party through the 2012  campaign is not going to die that does  not mean  that ron paul is creating some sort of  cult of personality uniquely among  politicians ron paul gets his fans  reading ron paul writes serious books of  political thought in political  philosophy and they become bestsellers  those books always have bibliographies  Ron Paul is always talking in his public  speeches about the thinkers who  influenced him whether it be the  Austrian economist Ludwig von Mises or  the 19th century French liberal Frederic  Bastiat and that's also why the Ron Paul  movement is going to have legs even when  Ron Paul is not on the political scene  anymore this is his last run for  president he's not going to be in  Congress anymore after this year he is  leaving in his wake a set of  institutions and a set of hundreds of  thousands of dedicated energized  intelligent youngsters who  unquestionably are going to shape  American politics moving down the line  even when Ron Paul is no longer there  leading the charge I think the most  meaningful historical analogy for the  role that Ron Paul and the Ron Paul  movement is going to play in the  Republican Party but now and in the  future is Barry Goldwater back in  nineteen sixty when he represented this  strongly anti-government force that was  driving the establishment crazy that was  overwhelmingly young overwhelmingly  energetic and that filled the party of  the degree that the party had to become  more respectful of his attitudes in the  future and then what you saw sixteen  years down the line was Ronald Reagan a  guy who had been out on the stump for  Barry Goldwater in 1964 is a  presidential candidate and I think  you're going t